WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:01.500
STEPHANIE WONG:
On the outside, it

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.140
might seem that people in
pageants just strut on stage

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.850
and wear really nice outfits.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.189
That is true, but
on top of that,

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:11.280
the pageant world today is made
up of extremely strong women

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.350
across all industries who are
doing some incredible work,

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:17.730
whether it's entrepreneurship or
fighting for a nonprofit cause.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.760
I'm Stephanie Wong,
and this is my journey

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.980
to becoming a
developer advocate.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.764
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.830
I got interested in beauty
pageants a little unexpectedly.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.380
I grew up in San Francisco,
where Miss Chinatown

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.650
USA has been a big part of the
Chinese culture for over 60

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:40.195
years.

00:00:40.195 --> 00:00:41.570
So I always looked
up to the idea

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.220
of maybe trying it one day.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.780
But it wasn't until
after college,

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:46.322
when I'd worked for
a couple of years

00:00:46.322 --> 00:00:48.530
and had established
myself in my career a bit

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.420
and was able to take
a couple weeks off,

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:53.600
that I decided to
make my first attempt.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.030
And when I got in, I
had zero expectations

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:57.635
of winning whatsoever.

00:00:57.635 --> 00:01:00.380
SPEAKER: Contestant number
four, Stephanie Wong

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:01.463
from Millbrae, California.

00:01:01.463 --> 00:01:03.088
STEPHANIE WONG: For
one of my pageants,

00:01:03.088 --> 00:01:04.819
I did aerial silks acrobatics.

00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:08.039
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:15.170
I also tried things like
Brazilian samba, Chinese dance,

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.180
and hip hop.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:21.380
So to my surprise,
I won the pageant.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.930
The biggest thing I learned
from doing beauty pageants

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.590
for the first time was
realizing how rewarding

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:31.550
it is to try things and get
out of your comfort zone.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.280
I performed a brand-new
talent that I never done

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.950
before, aerial silks, in
front of a new community

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:40.070
that I had never been
in front of, either.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:43.310
But it ended up being such
a life-changing experience

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:43.970
for me.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:49.320
One, I was extremely proud
of being an Asian-American.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.730
I was able to be an ambassador.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:54.680
But I was also able to meet
lifelong friends who are also

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:57.560
professionally experienced
and really successful

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.310
in all industries.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:03.710
So pageant experience has gotten
me to propel me in my career

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.620
by making me a great
speaker, standing up

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:09.080
for a cause I truly
believe in, and building

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:10.880
a community from the ground up.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.190
The community that I've
built have helped me

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.020
in my video creation
work in technology

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.080
because I'm able to leverage
a network, learn from them,

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.030
conduct workshops
alongside them,

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:23.160
and practice my communication
skills at a wide level.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.600
I absolutely love video creation
because of so many things

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:30.030
that I think have become
apparent in my life--

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.870
my love for performing,
my love for working

00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.840
with a team of really
talented people,

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.360
and having creative influence
from beginning to end.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.660
And I think that's something
that has been strung along

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.357
in my dance experience, along
with my pageant experience

00:02:44.357 --> 00:02:46.440
and a lot of the things
that I do outside of work.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.920
I am so inspired by
this work because I

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:51.830
am able to tap into
a community online

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:55.010
of learners and people who
come from varied backgrounds,

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:55.753
just like myself.

00:02:55.753 --> 00:02:57.920
If there's one thing that
I want people to take away

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.623
from my career, it's that
staying authentic will

00:03:00.623 --> 00:03:02.540
allow you to have a much
more fulfilling life,

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.900
and using your interests outside
of work to infuse your career

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.780
is going to enrich
your life overall.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:12.560
Having this rich life
outside of just my career

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.960
is so important to
making me the person

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.880
I am at the job every day.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.230
[MUSIC PLAYING]

